---
title: Prettier's style, at native speed
summary: tidy is a code formatter written in Rust. One binary prints what Prettier prints, for JavaScript, TypeScript, HTML, CSS, Markdown, YAML, JSON, TOML and more.
---

{{#var bench = $data.bench}}
{{#var total = bench.total}}
{{#var install = "curl -fsSL https://tidy.lukeed.com | sh"}}
{{#var claims = [
  [
    "Matches Prettier",
    "Checked on every release",
    "Against Prettier " +
      $data.release.prettier +
      " over a " +
      $utils.num(total.files) +
      "-file corpus: 100% of 3,906 JavaScript files and 3,308 of 3,309 TypeScript files.",
  ],
  [
    "Embedded code",
    "Formats the code inside your code",
    "Styles and scripts in HTML and Vue. Markdown code blocks and front matter. CSS, GraphQL, HTML and Markdown in JS template literals.",
  ],
  [
    "Config",
    "Configurable, if you need it",
    "Reads <code>tidy.json</code>, <code>tidy.jsonc</code> or <code>tidy.toml</code>, on top of <code>.editorconfig</code>. The defaults are Prettier&rsquo;s.",
  ],
  [
    "Stable",
    "Settles on the first run",
    "Where Prettier would change its mind on the next run, tidy prints where it settles, so <code>tidy check</code> stays green in CI.",
  ],
]}}
{{#var langs = [
  ["JavaScript, TypeScript, JSX", "Prettier"],
  ["HTML, Vue, Handlebars, MJML", "Prettier"],
  ["CSS, SCSS, Less", "Prettier"],
  ["JSON, JSONC, JSON5", "Prettier"],
  ["YAML, GraphQL, Markdown", "Prettier"],
  ["XML, SVG", "@prettier/plugin-xml"],
  ["TOML", "taplo"],
  ["Dockerfiles", "dprint-plugin-dockerfile"],
  ["INI, .editorconfig, .npmrc", "prettier-plugin-ini"],
]}}
<a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a>

<main id="main">
  <section class="hero band">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">A code formatter written in Rust</p>
        <h1>Prettier's style, at <mark>native speed</mark>.</h1>
        <p class="lede">One binary prints what Prettier prints, for JavaScript,
          TypeScript, HTML, CSS, Markdown, YAML, JSON, TOML and more. It does
          not shell out to Node, though there is a Node binding if you want one.</p>
        <div class="term">
          <em>$</em><code>{{ install }}</code><button
            class="copybtn"
            type="button"
            data-copy="{{ install }}"
          >copy</button>
        </div>
        <p class="alt">or build it with cargo &middot;
          <a href="/docs/install/">every way to install</a></p>
        <div class="controls">
          <a class="big" href="/docs/">Read the docs</a>
          <a class="big ghost" href="/playground/">Try the playground</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <tidy-hero class="card">
        <div class="cardbar">
          <span class="file">routes.ts</span>
          <span class="state tidy" data-state aria-live="polite">&#10003; tidy</span>
        </div>
        <div
          class="stage"
          data-stage
          role="img"
          aria-label="routes.ts reformatting from its messy original into Prettier style"
        >
          <pre data-mess>{{ $data.sample.mess }}</pre>
          <pre data-tidy>{{ $data.sample.tidy }}</pre>
        </div>
        <div class="cardfoot">
          <button class="replay" type="button" data-replay>
            <svg
              viewBox="0 0 24 24"
              fill="none"
              stroke="currentColor"
              stroke-width="2.6"
              stroke-linecap="round"
              stroke-linejoin="round"
              aria-hidden="true"
            ><path d="M20 11a8 8 0 1 0-2.3 6" /><path
                d="M20 4v7h-7"
              /></svg>replay
          </button>
        </div>
      </tidy-hero>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="speed band">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="kicker">{{ $utils.num(total.files) }} files, every language</p>
      <h2>{{ $utils.ms(total.prettier) }}
        <span class="arrow">&rarr;</span>
        {{ $utils.ms(total.tidy) }}</h2>
      <p class="sub">That's every language but XML, on an
        {{ bench.machine }}. The race below runs in real time. tidy is done
        before you notice it started.</p>

      <div
        class="race"
        data-race
        data-tidy="{{ total.tidy }}"
        data-prettier="{{ total.prettier }}"
        data-files="{{ $utils.num(total.files) }}"
      >
        <div class="lane me">
          <b>tidy</b>
          <div class="track"><i class="fill" data-fill="tidy"></i><span
              class="badge"
              data-badge
            >done!</span></div>
          <span class="t" data-time="tidy">{{ $utils.ms(total.tidy) }}</span>
        </div>
        <div class="lane them">
          <b>Prettier</b>
          <div class="track"><i class="fill" data-fill="prettier"></i></div>
          <span class="t" data-time="prettier">{{
              $utils.ms(total.prettier)
            }}</span>
        </div>
        <div class="racebar">
          <p data-race-note>{{ bench.speedup }}&times; faster over everything
            but XML.</p>
          <button class="big small" type="button" data-rerun>Race again</button>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="langs" data-langs>
        {{#each bench.featured as row}}
          {{#var group = $utils.bars(row)}}
          <div class="langgrp">
            <h3>{{ row.corpus }}<span>{{ $utils.num(row.files) }}
                files</span></h3>
            {{#each group.tools as bar, i}}
              <div class="b{{#if bar.me}} me{{/if}}">
                <span>{{ bar.who }}</span>
                <span class="tr"><i
                    style="width:{{ bar.width }}%;--n:{{ i }}"
                  ></i></span>
                <span class="ms">{{ $utils.ms(bar.ms) }}</span>
              </div>
            {{/each}}
            {{#if group.prettier}}
              <p class="slow">Prettier:
                {{ $utils.ms(group.prettier) }},
                <b>{{ group.slower }}&times; slower</b></p>
            {{/if}}
          </div>
        {{/each}}
      </div>

      <p class="note">{{ bench.machine }}, all cores, mean of both run orders.
        Bars compare the native tools; Prettier is off that scale.
        <a href="/docs/benchmarks/">Every language and the method &rarr;</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="why band">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="kicker">Why reach for it</p>
      <h2>Same output. Fewer surprises.</h2>
      <p class="sub">tidy's tests run Prettier over the same files and compare
        the bytes, so a difference is a bug, unless it's one of the
        <a href="/docs/deviations/">documented deviations</a>.</p>
      <div class="claims">
        {{#each claims as claim}}
          <article class="claim" tabindex="0"><span class="tag">{{
                claim[0]
              }}</span><h3>{{ claim[1] }}</h3><p>{{{ claim[2] }}}</p></article>
        {{/each}}
      </div>
      <p class="tidyhint">Hover or tap a card to straighten it up.</p>

      <div class="langwrap">
        <div>
          <p class="kicker">Languages</p>
          <h2>Every language Prettier formats</h2>
          <p class="sub">Plus the ones its plugins cover, built into the same
            binary. Nothing to install, nothing to register.</p>
        </div>
        <ul class="langlist">
          {{#each langs as lang}}
            <li>{{ lang[0] }} <span>{{ lang[1] }}</span></li>
          {{/each}}
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="cfgwrap">
        <p class="kicker">Config</p>
        <h2>Only when you want it</h2>
        <p class="sub">Each file takes the nearest
          <code>tidy.json</code>,
          <code>tidy.jsonc</code>
          or
          <code>tidy.toml</code>, on top of
          <code>.editorconfig</code>. Shared keys apply everywhere, and a
          language section overrides them. See
          <a href="/docs/options/">every option</a>.</p>
        <div class="cfg">
          <figure class="code"><div class="bar"><span
                class="file"
              >tidy.json</span></div>{{{ $data.sample.config }}}</figure>
          <div>
            <p class="then">Then run it</p>
            <figure class="code"><div class="bar"><span>Shell</span></div>{{{
                $data.sample.usage
              }}}</figure>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</main>

<footer class="foot band">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2>Run it on something <mark>messy</mark>.</h2>
    <div class="cta">
      <a class="big" href="/docs/">Read the docs</a>
      <a class="big ghost" href="/playground/">Try the playground</a>
    </div>
    <div class="fine">
      <a href="https://github.com/lukeed/tidy">GitHub</a>
      <a href="/docs/">Docs</a>
      <a href="/llms.txt">llms.txt</a>
      <span class="sp">MIT &copy; <a href="https://lukeed.com">lukeed</a></span>
    </div>
  </div>
</footer>